::STAT_U05_L02_QZ_Q01::
Question ID: STAT_U05_L02_QZ_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.DCR.3
Question:
A researcher randomly selects 20 students from each grade level. What sampling method is this?

{
=A. Stratified sample#Correct. The researcher samples from each grade-level subgroup.
~B. Cluster sample#Cluster sampling selects whole groups, not some people from every subgroup.
~C. Convenience sample#Convenience sampling uses whoever is easiest to reach.
~D. Census#A census collects data from the entire population.
}

::STAT_U05_L02_QZ_Q02::
Question ID: STAT_U05_L02_QZ_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.DCR.3
Question:
A researcher randomly selects 4 classrooms and surveys every student in those classrooms. What sampling method is this?

{
~A. Stratified sample#Stratified sampling would select from each subgroup, not whole selected classrooms.
=B. Cluster sample#Correct. Whole classrooms are selected as groups.
~C. Systematic sample#Systematic sampling uses a regular pattern after a starting point.
~D. Voluntary response sample#Voluntary response means people choose whether to respond.
}

::STAT_U05_L02_QZ_Q03::
Question ID: STAT_U05_L02_QZ_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.DCR.3
Question:
Which method is most likely to create convenience bias?

{
~A. Selecting every 10th name after a random start#Systematic sampling can be reasonable when the list has no hidden pattern.
~B. Randomly selecting from a complete list#A complete list and random selection reduce selection bias.
=C. Asking only people who are already near the survey table#Correct. This uses people who are easiest to reach, so some groups may be left out.
~D. Randomly selecting students from every grade#Random selection from every grade helps include important subgroups.
}

::STAT_U05_L02_QZ_Q04::
Question ID: STAT_U05_L02_QZ_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.DCR.3
Question:
What is the main difference between stratified and cluster sampling?

{
~A. They are identical methods#They are not identical because subgroup selection works differently.
~B. Stratified always uses volunteers, while cluster always uses a census#Neither method is defined by volunteers or a census.
~C. Cluster sampling never uses groups#Cluster sampling is specifically based on groups.
=D. Stratified samples from each subgroup, while cluster sampling selects whole groups#Correct. Both involve groups, but they use the groups differently.
}

